        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: The original circle has the equation \\(x^2 + y^2 = 25\\). To find the image of a point \\((x, y)\\) under reflection in the point \\((4, 1)\\), we use the midpoint formula. If \\((x', y')\\) is the image of \\((x, y)\\), then \\((4, 1)\\) is the midpoint of \\((x, y)\\) and \\((x', y')\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 620,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 621,
        "char_start": 285,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 253,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 254,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: Using the midpoint formula, we have:\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{x + x'}{2}, \\frac{y + y'}{2} \\right) = (4, 1)\n\\]\nThis gives us two equations:\n\\[\n\\frac{x + x'}{2} = 4 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\frac{y + y'}{2} = 1\n\\]\nSolving these, we get:\n\\[\nx + x' = 8 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad x' = 8 - x\n\\]\n\\[\ny + y' = 2 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad y' = 2 - y\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1065,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1066,
        "char_start": 623,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 465,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 466,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: Substitute \\(x' = 8 - x\\) and \\(y' = 2 - y\\) into the equation of the circle to find the equation of the image circle. The original circle's equation is \\(x^2 + y^2 = 25\\). Substituting \\(x = 8 - x'\\) and \\(y = 2 - y'\\) into this equation, we get:\n\\[\n(8 - x')^2 + (2 - y')^2 = 25\n\\]\nExpanding and simplifying:\n\\[\n64 - 16x' + x'^2 + 4 - 4y' + y'^2 = 25\n\\]\n\\[\nx'^2 + y'^2 - 16x' - 4y' + 68 = 25\n\\]\n\\[\nx'^2 + y'^2 - 16x' - 4y' + 43 = 0\n\\]"
      },
      {
